statement:
Let X be a topological space (universe u; no separation axiom needed). Let μ be a Radon outer measure on X in the sense of Simon Def. 4.6 (Lean IsRadonOuterMeasure μ):
- (R1) μ is Borel regular — every Borel set is μ-measurable and every set has a Borel superset of equal measure — and μ(K) < ∞ for every compact K;
- (R2) μ(A) = inf{μ(U) : U open ⊇ A};
- (R3) μ(U) = sup{μ(K) : K compact ⊆ U} for open U.
Let μ̄ := caratheodoryMeasure μ be μ restricted to the σ-algebra 𝓜_μ of μ-measurable (Carathéodory) sets (Lemma 1.6/Remark 1.7). Then every continuous f : X → ℝ with compact support (f ∈ C_c(X, ℝ)) is μ̄-integrable.
